 `seed` upserts modules and lessons. Ids derive from slugs, so re-seeding never breaks learner progress. A lesson removed from the Markdown is removed from its module too.
+
+When the database holds an older copy of a module under the same slug with another id (lessons imported before `seed` existed, for example), `seed` skips that module and reports a conflict, and the site keeps serving the old lessons. Take it over with `--adopt`:
+
+```bash
+DATABASE_URL=... pnpm exec tsx scripts/seed.ts --adopt misingi-ya-nuru
+```
+
+Learner progress moves to the lesson with the same slug, classes list the new module, and the old module is deleted once it is empty.
